{"name":"Covent Garden","hex":"#86b097","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Covent Garden","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A district in central London, England .","The Royal Opera House, Covent Garden"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A farthing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Covent_Garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Covent Garden","blocks":[{"text":"Covent Garden is a district in London, on the eastern fringes of the West End, between St Martin's Lane and Drury Lane. It is associated with the former fruit-and-vegetable market in the central square, now a popular shopping and tourist site, and with the Royal Opera House, itself known as \"Covent Garden\". The district is divided by the main thoroughfare of Long Acre, north of which is given over to independent shops centred on Neal's Yard and Seven Dials, while the south contains the central square with its street performers and most of the historical buildings, theatres and entertainment facilities, including the London Transport Museum and the Theatre Royal, Drury Lane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Covent_Garden_Interior_May_2006_crop.jpg/330px-Covent_Garden_Interior_May_2006_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Covent_Garden","wikidata":"Q55019"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden","w